A||N||3||Nyte||Cleaning inside of fuel tank...||||1||
Z||000000||Nyte||05-07-2001||03:42 AM||||How hard is it to take the fuel tank off the car?  I've read somewhere when I was interested in rebuilding a 77 Chevy CK that an owner of one of those trucks took off the tank and had some radiator guy put some kind of fluid inside and cleaned all sorts of gunk out.  It's been awhile since I read it and forgotten the details... with this being an eightteen year old car, is there some sort of process I could do to the same effect?<P>Plus I'm probably going to have to drop the tank anyways because my fuel gauge isn't correct and father thinks it might be problem inside the tank.<P>------------------<BR><B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B><BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><P>"Damned '84 econo coupes!  Why didn't you guys tell me this BEFORE I bought the dang thing!"||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||05-07-2001||09:19 AM||||If I remember correctly from about 2 years ago, it wasn't terribly hard, but we had a lift to get the car over our heads... We had to loosen the exhaust sytem and then it was pretty easy, long as you have a couple strong people to support the tank when its not secured anymore.<P>Sorry I can't give you more details, I know its not a huge deal to do though.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||05-07-2001||10:17 AM||||i've done it a couple times. once with ramps and once with jack stands.if you can get as much gas out as possible and don't mind getting really dirty (i don't have a garage. did it on rock drives both times), it's not too bad. i raised the rear of the car got it up just high enough to slide it out from the rear.<P>   the second time the car had a bad tank. plenty rusty. a couple of radiator shops wanted about $100 to coat the tank but i ended up getting another in real good condition from kick hill. $50 plus shipping.<P>i also just this weekend coated a motorcycle tank. i think with the baffleing in the fiero tank a good coating would be hard to achieve. the kit i used had some pre coating cleaning solution that said they would harm plastic (maybe a pro place uses something else), plus it was good for just up to a 5 gallon tank so you'd need two kits. $30 a kit.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||05-07-2001||10:54 AM||||I lift one side of the car and take it out the side, Never touched the exhaust. takes less than 2 hours out and back in.||||reg||1
